---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Changelog — devjoe Garmin" description="Release history for devjoe Garmin apps.">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Release history</p>
      <h1>Changelog</h1>
      <p class="lede">Public changes begin with the first Production release. Beta work remains explicitly marked.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="content-grid">
      <aside>Burnished Sky Ahead</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="status-tag">Production candidate · 1.6.0</p>
        <h2>1.6.0 — Status, kept in its place</h2>
        <p><strong>Prepared August 27, 2026 · Garmin submission pending</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Adds a unified alarm and Do Not Disturb status rail beside the time.</li>
          <li>Adds a default-off Show notification count setting and caps the visible count at <code>99+</code>.</li>
          <li>Uses display-native AMOLED and MIP status icons while keeping status indicators out of AOD.</li>
          <li>Improves resilience during in-place Connect IQ Store updates.</li>
          <li>Keeps permissions and the existing 48-product compatibility list unchanged.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.5.0</p>
        <h2>1.5.0 — Native MIP across three sizes</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 24, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Adds a purpose-built 280 × 280 MIP layout for Enduro 3, fēnix 7X / Enduro 2, fēnix 7X Pro, and fēnix 8 Solar 51mm families.</li>
          <li>Adds the native 240 × 240 layout to Forerunner 245 Music and expands the 260 × 260 layout to fēnix 6 / 6 Pro, vívoactive 4, First Avenger, and Darth Vader.</li>
          <li>Keeps the MIP outlook deliberately compact: three values paired with 3H, using temperature or precipitation percentage as conditions require.</li>
          <li>Leaves AMOLED layouts, Outdoor Brief, Weather Signals, animation, and AOD behavior unchanged.</li>
          <li>Keeps Forerunner 255S and Approach S62 unsupported.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.4.0</p>
        <h2>1.4.0 — Native MIP 260 support</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 24, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Adds a native sunlight-readable 260 × 260 MIP design for Forerunner 255 / 255 Music, Forerunner 955 / 955 Solar, fēnix 7 / quatix 7, fēnix 7 Pro, fēnix 7 Pro Solar without Wi-Fi, and fēnix 8 Solar 47mm.</li>
          <li>Uses a dedicated 64-color palette, compact typography, and complete three-value 3H forecast instead of scaling the AMOLED face.</li>
          <li>Keeps all existing AMOLED layouts and low-power behavior unchanged.</li>
          <li>Adds optional Outdoor Brief and Weather Signals experiences on supported AMOLED watches; both remain Off by default.</li>
          <li>Excludes Forerunner 255S and unlisted legacy MIP models.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.3.1</p>
        <h2>1.3.1 — Store update resilience</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 16, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Improves resilience during Connect IQ Store updates.</li>
          <li>Keeps the watch-face appearance, settings, permissions, and supported-device list unchanged.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.3.0</p>
        <h2>1.3.0 — Broader AMOLED compatibility</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 15, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Adds Forerunner 165 / 165 Music, Venu 2 / Venu 2 Plus, vívoactive 5, and epix (Gen 2) / quatix 7 Sapphire compatibility.</li>
          <li>Adds the discreet alarm-enabled indicator beside the weekday.</li>
          <li>Improves forecast typography on compact and no-vector-font AMOLED displays.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.2.1</p>
        <h2>1.2.1 — More reliable updates</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 14, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Improves reliability when applying or updating the watch face.</li>
          <li>Adds startup safeguards for forecast data and display resources.</li>
          <li>Keeps the approved appearance, settings, and supported-device list unchanged.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.2.0</p>
        <h2>1.2.0 — More watches, clearer alarm status</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 14, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Adds Venu 4 41/45mm, Venu 3/3S, vívoactive 6, Forerunner 170 Music, Instinct 3 AMOLED 45mm, and D2 Air X15 compatibility.</li>
          <li>Adds a discreet indicator beside the weekday when Garmin reports an alarm on supported devices.</li>
          <li>Keeps the indicator hidden in AOD and does not infer a next alarm time or exact count.</li>
          <li>Uses the existing 390 × 390 and 454 × 454 layouts; the Instinct 3 AMOLED 45mm uses the no-vector-font fallback.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-tag">Production · previous release 1.1.1</p>
        <h2>1.1.1 — Forecast clock labels</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 13, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Labels each forecast node with its represented local clock hour.</li>
          <li>Shows the current weather condition directly, without a location or provider reveal.</li>
          <li>Refreshes the Store imagery and explanation for the lower-left forecast timeline.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>1.1.0 — Premium AMOLED expansion</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 13, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Adds selected fēnix 8, fēnix 8 Pro, fēnix E, epix Pro (Gen 2), and Forerunner 965 product IDs.</li>
          <li>Publishes Simulator validation separately from FR970 physical evidence.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>1.0.0 — Initial release</h2>
        <p><strong>Released August 11, 2026</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Day and night compositions with contextual current weather.</li>
          <li>Three-node rain, snow, mixed-precipitation, and temperature forecasts.</li>
          <li>Five AOD ornaments, three weather-frame styles, and optional wake animation.</li>
          <li>Honest fallbacks for missing weather, heart-rate, and forecast data.</li>
          <li>Nine selected round AMOLED Garmin launch products.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
